      <h2>Biography</h2>

      <p>
        I am a Ph.D. Candidate in Industrial &amp; Systems Engineering at
        Mississippi State University. My research combines machine learning,
        mathematical optimization, computer vision, and intelligent system design.
      </p>

      <p>
        I am particularly interested in developing methods that connect rigorous
        learning objectives with domain knowledge and practical decision requirements.
        My work has included applications in manufacturing quality monitoring,
        medical imaging, agricultural robotics, and data-driven decision systems.
      </p>

      <p>
        Alongside research, I have experience in teaching, student mentoring,
        interdisciplinary collaboration, research software development, and
        translating technical ideas into deployable systems.
      </p>
